WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.360
- What sort of thing do you like to eat?

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:04.360
- Excellent question.

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:09.360
Green eggs and ham, it's
the dish that cannot mish.

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:11.170
- I'm vegan.

00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:15.620
- Oh, I'm so sorry, I didn't realize.

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:16.740
How long have you known?

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:17.573
- [Sam] Try some?

00:00:17.573 --> 00:00:18.493
- Ugh, no.

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:22.460
- They're surprisingly
good with the mouse.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:24.560
- I will not eat them with a mouse.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:26.210
I'm fine without mush.

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:29.471
- I don't want to eat them
either, you filthy son of a

00:00:29.471 --> 00:00:30.710
(squeaking)
(giggling)

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:32.530
- Captain Bigman, we were taken out

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:35.713
by a dastardly band of
accomplices armed with WMDs.

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:39.519
- Weaponized melon devices?

00:00:39.519 --> 00:00:40.998
- It was cantaloupe!

00:00:40.998 --> 00:00:43.415
Oh, the horror, the disguise!

00:00:44.329 --> 00:00:45.536
- The garbage fruit.

00:00:45.536 --> 00:00:46.369
(glass breaking)

00:00:46.369 --> 00:00:48.910
It's like 90% of every fruit salad.

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:50.220
- I know, right?

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:51.890
- And if Sandra knew I took the--

00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:53.180
- Oh, right, your chick.

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:54.970
- Sandra is no one's chick.

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:57.860
She's very much her own
hen and I respect that.

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:01.000
- From one feminist to
another, that's very admirable.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.390
- Gosh, it doesn't even
feel like we're moving.

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:06.402
- Oh, the park and ride
is deceptively fast.

00:01:06.402 --> 00:01:09.440
(upbeat music)

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:13.848
- Why did you drive your car into a lake?

00:01:13.848 --> 00:01:15.930
- Oh, it wasn't my car.

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:17.430
It belonged to the bad guys.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:19.665
They would have tracked
it, so I had to lake it.

00:01:19.665 --> 00:01:23.311
What's important is that nobody got hurt.

00:01:23.311 --> 00:01:25.573
Everybody's safe.

00:01:25.573 --> 00:01:27.117
(playful music)
- Hey kids!

00:01:27.117 --> 00:01:28.839
- [Kids] Daddy!

00:01:28.839 --> 00:01:30.993
- Did it just get dark all of a sudden?

00:01:32.032 --> 00:01:34.287
- (screaming) Swim for your lives!

00:01:34.287 --> 00:01:35.562
(screaming)

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:39.986
(crashing)
(bubbling)

00:01:39.986 --> 00:01:41.550
(crying)

00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:43.470
- No harm, no foul.

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:44.760
- [Mother Fish] Let's get a head count.

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:46.090
- Can we get more blankets over here?

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:48.894
- One fish, two fish, and
there's red fish and blue.

00:01:48.894 --> 00:01:51.781
(suspenseful music)

00:01:51.781 --> 00:01:54.770
(squeaking)
(lively music)

00:01:54.770 --> 00:01:56.783
- The guard is on duty.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:00.830
Everything is under control, including me.

00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:03.110
- A fox guarding the henhouse?

00:02:03.110 --> 00:02:05.130
Well, that's progressive.

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:07.410
Woo, we're home free.

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:10.203
Everyone knows goats can't climb.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:12.640
(yelling)

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:14.430
- What kind of wildlife expert are you?

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:16.580
Goats are known especially
for their climbing.

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:18.790
- That is an outdated stereotype

00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:20.420
and I prefer not to perpetuate it.

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:22.590
- You haven't even evolved as a species

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:24.065
and you think you're better than us?

00:02:24.065 --> 00:02:25.700
(screaming)
- [All] Huh?

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:27.860
- You still live in a shabby nest

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:32.215
made of mud and leaves
and who knows what else.

00:02:32.215 --> 00:02:33.048
(grunting)
And I mean, you seem

00:02:33.048 --> 00:02:35.800
to have a remedial
semblance of a social order,

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:37.360
but you're hardly civilized.

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:39.824
Have you even developed an alphabet?

00:02:39.824 --> 00:02:41.582
(grunting)
- Keep doing that.

00:02:41.582 --> 00:02:42.868
(growling)

00:02:42.868 --> 00:02:44.137
- Keep doing what?

00:02:44.137 --> 00:02:48.249
- Whatever that is,
keep doing it. (yelling)

00:02:48.249 --> 00:02:49.082
(growling)

00:02:49.082 --> 00:02:51.415
(screaming)

00:02:55.083 --> 00:02:57.923
- Seriously, what have
you done with your lives?

00:02:59.062 --> 00:03:00.626
(screaming)

00:03:00.626 --> 00:03:03.203
♪ I lived a life of humble joys ♪

00:03:03.203 --> 00:03:08.203
♪ My wife and child were my salvation ♪

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:14.009
♪ It was a time of poverty ♪

00:03:14.009 --> 00:03:18.433
♪ That starved both man and mouse across ♪

00:03:18.433 --> 00:03:20.850
♪ The nation ♪

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:24.440
- [Narrator] Sam and Guy crawled through

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:27.454
five fuzzball fields of funk

00:03:27.454 --> 00:03:28.340
(splashing)

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:30.799
and they finally made their way out.

00:03:30.799 --> 00:03:32.726
(chuckling) Who'da thunk?

00:03:32.726 --> 00:03:35.543
- (laughing) Do you feel that rain, Guy?

00:03:36.429 --> 00:03:38.596
That sweet cleansing rain!

